# The base images /upgrade's two-stage release runs on the host it deploys to, by digest (.claude/skills/upgrade/SKILL.md,
# "Two-stage release"). docker-compose.yml puts ORBIT_REGISTRY in front of each, so the target pulls them from that
# registry, which holds them under Docker Hub's own path: library/<name>. Each digest is a multi-platform index, copied
# whole. A digest changes only here, in a commit, so a release and its rollback both name the base images they ran with.
#
# A new digest has to reach the registry before a release names it, from the registry's host:
#   docker run --rm --network host quay.io/skopeo/stable copy --all --preserve-digests --dest-tls-verify=false \
#     docker://docker.io/library/<name>@<digest> docker://<ORBIT_REGISTRY>/library/<name>:<version>
#
# PostgreSQL is not here. deploy/postgres-pinned.yml pins postgres and pgbackup by digest (16.14), and so does
# deploy/db-proxy.yml its HAProxy, each from ORBIT_REGISTRY; the deploy ships both with the release, and the target lists
# them in COMPOSE_FILE. One pin per image: the deploy stage refuses a release whose postgres is not the registry's.
#
# nginx 1.31.1 on Alpine, the web gateway.
ORBIT_NGINX_IMAGE=library/nginx@sha256:8b1e78743a03dbb2c95171cc58639fef29abc8816598e27fb910ed2e621e589a
# NATS 2.15.1 on Alpine, the runner link's message bus.
ORBIT_NATS_IMAGE=library/nats@sha256:7ae34c25dfd6fe2e01c6483eabef20d796690fdcac6c4d94ca780a6cf9877fde
